DSHOptimizeMosire · dsh-subagent-access
=======================================

This package adds a parent → child sub-agent control surface to DeepSeek
Harness (DSH) profiles: list, message, and interrupt the sub-agent sessions a
top-level session started. It is not an official DeepSeek package and is not
affiliated with or endorsed by DeepSeek.

Official extension points only
------------------------------
The plugin is implemented entirely with public DSH extension points:

- the `ctx.subagents` service (`listChildren` / `sendMessage` / `interrupt`);
- the `ctx.agents` registry (`get` / `list`) and each Agent's live status;
- per-Agent tool registration through `agent.ctx.tools.register` and the
  official `defineTool` helper from `@deepseek-ai/dsh-tools`;
- the `agent/created` and `agent/disposed` lifecycle events.

No DSH source code was copied into this package. The three tools are
deliberately named differently from the Agent Team tools (`send_message` /
`list_agents` / `interrupt_agent`): this bundle neither modifies Agent Team nor
duplicates its behaviour. It is a Host plugin loaded through a bundle patch and
does not modify any DSH package.

Workspace module resolution
---------------------------
The workspace package has no npm dependencies. Its single official import
(`@deepseek-ai/dsh-tools`) resolves through the symlink farm that
`tools/link-dsh-peers.mjs` creates in `node_modules/@deepseek-ai/`, pointing at
the running DSH installation so both sides share one module instance.

